  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="e1f655a9-5546-46d4-81b3-34e1ab3db3b0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each equation in questions 1 – 5, identify the values of \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) that you would substitute into the quadratic formula to solve the equation.</para><para>\(3x^2+8x+4=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?<para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=3\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=3\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_22cc9439-d99f-49f6-9c8d-cbb0077c8c5e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?<para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=8\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=8\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_215ae2af-15d1-4e4d-b781-21865a8636a6" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=4\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=4\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_9ceb36b1-9646-4a28-9444-576bfe8549c5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(2x^2−5x+2=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=2\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_08e782a8-c00c-4c0c-a71b-174e096f3270" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=-5\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=-5\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="edfdc15e-7642-4367-a4c7-eb9bef34bcc4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\) .</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=2\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="fa55ea19-921c-43e3-8094-cfd005e3bfb5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(-9x^2+13x−1=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=-9\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=-9\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_57a376bf-67ff-470e-9333-13ca18ac0400" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=13\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=13\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_07423fbb-b45e-4260-889d-6408161d11b7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=-1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=-1\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e76ed883-01aa-4c08-86e7-db90137bb2b0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(x^2+x−11=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=1\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_600c4806-8237-4672-ba70-4ce867334a0a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=1\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_28f83b83-5229-445f-b8c3-3875d1804f49" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=-11\)
     </para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=-11\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_25fe22a4-1dfc-4dba-bb76-3dbe28c1ac1f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(-x^2+16x+64=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=-1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=-1\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="b7cb9b8e-e30e-4ba1-ad0b-6572fb1dc420" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=16\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=16\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_1c6a0962-99d3-4e56-8d1d-a4478ca972d4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=64\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=64\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="f77864d2-e184-434a-a512-d0802a423684" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each equation, use the quadratic formula to solve the equation, then choose the correct<emphasis>two</emphasis> solutions for \(x\).</para>
      <para>\(x^2+9x+20=0\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(x=-4, x=-5\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.6.3 and 9.6.4.</para><para>The correct answers are: \(x=-4, x=-5\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c0bb28e4-e143-47f8-a065-fbd13b34ea2f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(x^2−10x+21=0\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(x=3, x=7\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.6.3 and 9.6.4.</para><para>The correct answers are: \(x=3, x=7\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="fbc3e043-7ebc-4cf4-92f8-54248608bc2a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(3x^2−5x+1=0\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(x=\frac{5}{6}+\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\), \(x=\frac{5}{6}-\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.6.3 and 9.6.4.</para><para>The correct answers are: \(x=\frac{5}{6}+\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\), \(x=\frac{5}{6}-\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_6e01f147-e0df-4960-869d-718a09ea39c7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each equation for questions 7  – 12, identify the values of \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) that you would substitute into the quadratic formula to solve the equation.</para><para>\(x^2+9x+18=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=1\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e75627c2-3b1f-4344-949a-9aef9b84e8e2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=9\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=9\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c18d7b39-0a6c-4102-82e4-5b6894eeec43" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=18\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=18\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_92fd8bb8-73af-48d5-8678-1ad81744f390" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4x^2−3x+11=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=4\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=4\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_2bc5dc8f-fca9-4bdd-a45a-b71e8160b560" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=-3\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=-3\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="f647527e-e41f-4595-89c1-42aea6fc9f4f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=11\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=11\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_6d8df732-cdd4-4245-b106-1e7428c7f284" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(81−x+5x^2=0\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=5\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=5\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d244ee3c-d0b7-4c06-b0ec-2dfa5b8881cb" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=-1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=-1\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="baae3a5b-f8aa-4617-a6af-37076c5acd4b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=81\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=81\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_48847e59-9a04-4ada-bbf8-4070efbc603b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(45x^2+3x=\frac{1}{3}\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=45\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=45\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="b78f9b5c-7728-4210-981e-6baba4cd6862" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=3\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=3\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d04a3843-2d96-4a31-8e09-09796c5223c7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
       </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(-\frac13\)</para><para>\(\frac13\)</para><para>1</para><para>0</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=-\frac13\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=-\frac13\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_53746598-cb29-4919-85db-b743afeb2ec9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(121=x^2\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=1-\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="ae390100-f322-43e4-be22-8804bef9ed1f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=0\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=0\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="dbf65de3-3a2c-4250-ae6d-a11d472dbd55" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(c\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=-121\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(c=-121\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c828d2d2-2a85-436f-bacd-4479b1450125" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(7x+14x^2=42\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of \(a\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(a\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a=14\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(a=14\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_731b3fba-4c6e-4bc4-96ad-5d6b8a837613" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of \(b\)?
          <para>Enter the value of \(b\).</para>
       </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b=7\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b=7\).
